Z||000000||Deer_Slayer||01-10-2000||03:26 PM||||A while back, I was at a junkyard looking for parts for an 86 SE I am working on.  There, there were 6 wrecks (one with a Holley valve cover and high performance sparkplug wires).  One of the cars was a Fiero Indy.  I did not get to take a good look at the car since there was nothing to get from it.  By the front end, it was either an 86 or newer.  The guy at the junkyard called it a "rare bird".  Can anwone give me some more information about this type of Fiero?||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||01-10-2000||03:46 PM||||The indy Fiero was only made for one year, 1984. The car came with an aero front fascia, and was a regular notchback at the rear. Engine used was the regular 4-cyl. Was only one of two models to come with a wing standard. The rear decklid said "Indy Fiero". There was also a steel "Indy Fiero" front emblem. There was a dealer installable option to have "Official Pace Car" on both doors. Came standard with 14" wheels. Had sierra grey leather bolsters w/red cloth insert, indy 500 logo into back insert. There were only 2001 Indys made, but that number is always in dispute. The indy was only available in white, and had matching door mounted mirrors and wheels.<BR>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
